# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Cancelling target selection aborts Goblin Cratermaker's activated ability before costs are paid.
# Forcing: One creature per side keeps the damage-mode target domain small and reaches one bounded target prompt.
# AI behavior: The scenario stops after the human cancels; the opponent has no decision.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = The browser cancels back to priority with Goblin Cratermaker and Mountain unchanged.
#   LOSE = The ability resolves or the turn limit expires.
#   TIMEOUT = Target cancellation does not return to priority.
# Card roles:
#   Goblin Cratermaker — supplies a modal targeted ability with mana and sacrifice costs.
#   Grizzly Bears — supplies an opposing legal target for the damage mode.
#   Mountain — pays the generic activation cost and keeps both libraries non-empty.
# Protocol path: ActionsAvailableReq -> CastingTimeOptionsReq -> SelectTargetsReq with Abort -> CancelActionReq -> priority state.

[metadata]
Name:Goblin Cratermaker Cancel
Goal:Survive
Turns:2
Difficulty:Easy
Description:Start Goblin Cratermaker's damage ability, then cancel target selection before paying its costs.

[state]
ActivePlayer=Human
ActivePhase=Main1
HumanLife=20
AILife=20

humanbattlefield=Goblin Cratermaker;Mountain
humanlibrary=Mountain
aibattlefield=Grizzly Bears
ailibrary=Mountain
